## 0. Definitions/Preambule

- **"The Mod"** refers to this software as released by the Author,
  including its source code, compiled/binary forms, and any assets
  (textures, models, sounds, configuration files, documentation)
  distributed with it.

- **"Covered Work"** means the Mod or any Modified Version of it, in
  whole or in substantial part, in source or binary form.

- **"You"** refers to any individual or entity exercising rights under
  this license.

- **"The Author"** refers to the original copyright holder(s) of the
  Mod, named above. Where this license requires the Author's
  permission, only the Author — not the developer of any Modified
  Version, and not any other party — may grant it.

- **"Substantive Modification"** means a change to the Mod that adds,
  removes, or meaningfully alters functionality, features, behavior,
  compatibility, or content, and that a reasonable person would
  regard as having genuine independent value to users beyond
  qualifying the work for Distribution under this license.

  The following are never Substantive Modifications, alone or in
  combination: renaming files, classes, variables, or the mod itself;
  changing version strings, metadata, branding, credits, default
  configuration values, or cosmetic details of trivial scope;
  recompiling, repackaging, re-obfuscating, minifying, or
  re-formatting the code; translating comments or documentation;
  adding non-functional code, unused assets, or filler content; or
  disabling, stubbing, or trivially toggling existing features.

  **Anti-circumvention rule**: a change whose primary purpose is to
  cause a work to qualify as a Modified Version, or otherwise to evade
  Section 2, 4, or 5, is not a Substantive Modification, regardless of
  its technical nature. The burden of proving that a
  modification is Substantive lies with the person Distributing the
  work.

- **"Unmodified Copy"** means a Covered Work that contains no
  Substantive Modification relative to a release by the Author.

- **"Modified Version"** means a work based on the Mod that contains
  at least one Substantive Modification relative to the Mod as
  released by the Author. A verbatim or substantively identical copy
  of someone else's Modified Version is a copy of that Modified
  Version, and its Distribution is governed by Section 3, including
  the attribution obligations to both the Author and that Modified
  Version's developer.

- **"Major Derivative"** means a Modified Version whose Substantive
  Modifications constitute substantial independent engineering or
  creative work by its developer, such as: (a) a port to a different
  mod loader or framework (for example, between Forge, NeoForge,
  or Quilt) requiring significant reimplementation; (b) a port
  to a different game, game edition, or platform; (c) a maintained
  continuation or rewrite across a major game-version boundary
  requiring significant reimplementation; or (d) the addition of
  substantial original features or content that (i) required
  independent creative or engineering effort comparable to the
  foregoing, (ii) constitutes the primary value of the Modified
  Version to its users beyond that of the original Mod, and (iii) was
  authored by the developer claiming Major Derivative status (bundled
  third-party code, libraries, assets, or bulk procedurally-generated
  content do not count toward this threshold). Minor patches,
  configuration changes, small feature additions, and ports achieved
  chiefly through automated remapping, transpilation, or existing
  compatibility layers do not qualify. In case of dispute, the
  burden of proving Major Derivative status lies with the
  developer claiming it.

  The "developer" of a Major Derivative may be an individual, an
  informal team, or a legal entity; where it is a team or entity, the
  rights this license grants to that developer are held by the team or
  entity as a whole and may be exercised by members acting on its
  behalf, but remain non-transferable to anyone outside it.

- **"Authorized Platform"** means a distribution platform, website,
  launcher, or hosting service (for example, CurseForge or Modrinth)
  on which the Author has officially published the Mod and continues
  to make it publicly available. Whether a platform is an Authorized
  Platform is determined per platform, not per company or brand: a
  platform on which the Author has not published the Mod is not an
  Authorized Platform even if the Author has published the Mod
  elsewhere. A platform ceases to be an Authorized Platform,
  prospectively, when the Author removes the Mod from it or publicly
  declares it unauthorized. The Author may maintain a list of
  Authorized Platforms on the Mod's official project page or
  repository; where such a list exists, it is authoritative.

- **"Distribute"** means to make a Covered Work available to any third
  party, whether publicly or within any group, platform, server,
  repository, launcher, or community, in source or binary form,
  whether or not for compensation. Private Sharing (defined below) and
  Server Operation (defined below) are not Distribution.

- **"Private Sharing"** means providing a copy of a Covered Work, free
  of any charge, to no more than 10 individuals in total within any
  rolling twelve-month period, each of whom is identified to you by
  name and is actively engaged with you in joint development, testing,
  or code review of that work. This cap counts every individual who
  receives a copy during the period, whether or not they remain a
  collaborator; rotating, replacing, or cycling recipients does not
  reset it. Private Sharing conveys "no right to share further":
  recipients may not Distribute or further privately share the copy,
  and must obtain any further rights under this license directly
  (e.g., by obtaining the work from an authorized public source).
  Posting a copy in any channel, group, server, or repository
  accessible to persons beyond those named individuals is
  Distribution, not Private Sharing.

- **"Server Operation"** means running a Covered Work on a game
  server, host, or service such that third parties interact with its
  functionality. Server Operation includes automatically transmitting
  an exact copy of the Covered Work, as obtained from an authorized
  source, to a player's client solely to enable that player to
  connect to and play on that server (for example, via a server
  resource/mod sync system, launcher profile, or connection-time
  download). Such transmission is not Distribution and is not
  prohibited Compensation even if the server itself charges for
  access, provided the copy is not otherwise charged for, gated,
  modified, rebranded, or made available for general download beyond
  what connecting to the server requires.

- **"Compensation"** means money or anything of monetary value,
  including sale proceeds, fees, subscriptions, mandatory donations,
  paywalled or tiered access, early-access privileges, advertising or
  affiliate revenue attributable to hosting or linking the work,
  platform creator revenue-share payments, and in-kind consideration.

- **"Complete Corresponding Source"** means the preferred form of the
  work for making modifications to it, including all source code,
  original (non-flattened, non-baked) asset files where they exist,
  build scripts, and instructions sufficient for a competent developer
  to build the distributed binary. Obfuscated, transpiled, decompiled,
  or partial source does not qualify.

- **"Written Permission"** means an explicit, recorded grant of
  permission from the Author, identifying the grantee and the specific
  acts permitted. Written Permission is non-transferable, applies only
  to the acts it explicitly states, and may contain conditions. The
  Author may maintain a public record of grants at
  https://github.com/Kombucha-Works/Create-Security/blob/main/Author's%20Grants;
  a claimed grant that the Author disputes and that does not
  appear in that record (where one is maintained) is presumed invalid.
  A forged or misattributed grant is void and conveys nothing.

## 1. Basic Permissions

You are free to, provided that all terms and condition stated herein will be fullfilled:

- Download, install, and use the Mod for any personal purpose.
- View, study, and modify the source code, and patch, edit, or
  reconfigure binary forms, for your own use.
- Engage in Private Sharing as defined in Preambule.
- Engage in Server Operation, including on servers that charge for
  access or are otherwise monetized, provided you do not charge for,
  or condition anything of value on, providing copies of the Covered
  Work's files themselves.
- Quote short excerpts of the source code for the purposes of
  commentary, education, tutorials, compatibility documentation, or
  review, with attribution.

These permissions are granted royalty-free and do not expire, provided
you comply with the all terms and conditions mentioned in this license.

## 2. Distribution of Unmodified Copies

You may not Distribute an Unmodified Copy without prior Written
Permission from the Author. This includes, without limitation:

- Re-uploading or mirroring the Mod on any website, platform,
  launcher, repository, or file host.
- Bundling the Mod into modpacks, plugin collections, launchers, or
  server distributions, except as expressly permitted by the
  modpack bundling permission in Section 5.
- Distributing works whose only changes are non-substantive (see
  Preambule above) — such works are Unmodified Copies regardless of
  superficial differences, renaming, or repackaging.

For inclusion in a free modpack distributed on an Authorized
Platform, no Written Permission is required — see the modpack
bundling permission in Section 5. For any other mirroring or bundling
of an Unmodified Copy (for example, archival re-hosting, or modpack
distribution on a platform where the Author has not published the
Mod), contact the Author to request Written Permission.

**Sunset (abandonment) provision:** if, for a continuous period of
three (3) years, the Author has (a) published no release, update, or public
statement regarding the Mod, and (b) been unreachable despite
reasonable, documented attempts at contact through the channels listed
in the Mod's official repository or project page, then Written
Permission is deemed granted to all persons to Distribute Unmodified
Copies of the Mod, free of any charge and subject to Sections 3(c),
3(e), and 4. This deemed permission terminates prospectively — without
affecting copies already Distributed under it — if the Author returns
and publicly revokes it. Nothing in this license transfers copyright
or any other right reserved to the Author.

## 3. Distribution of Modified Versions

You may Distribute a Modified Version — whether one you created or a
verbatim copy of one created by someone else — free of any
Compensation (except as Section 4 expressly permits for the developer
of a Major Derivative), without prior permission, provided that
all of the following conditions are met:

a. **Source availability** — You must make the Complete Corresponding
   Source of the Modified Version available (i) at no charge beyond
   reasonable physical distribution costs, (ii) from the same location
   and by the same general means as the binary, (iii) beginning no
   later than the moment the binary is first made available, and
   (iv) for as long as you continue to offer the binary. Access to the
   source may not be conditioned on payment, registration beyond a
   hosting platform's ordinary free account, surveys, ad-gates, or any
   barrier prohibited by Section 4.

b. **Documented changes** — You must clearly state that the work is
   modified and provide a reasonably detailed, accurate description of
   the Substantive Modifications, in the source code, a changelog, or
   accompanying documentation. If you are redistributing someone
   else's Modified Version, you must preserve their change
   documentation.

c. **Attribution** — You must retain a clear, visible credit to the
   Author as the creator of the original Mod, including a link to (or
   citation of) the original source repository, in both the source
   code and any user-facing description (e.g., project page, mod
   description, README). If Distributing someone else's Modified
   Version, you must also retain that developer's credits. You must
   not present any Covered Work in a way that implies it is the
   original Mod or is endorsed by the Author.

d. **License pass-through** — The Modified Version must be licensed in
   its entirety under this same license, including these same
   restrictions on Compensation and on Unmodified Copies. You may not
   add terms that remove, narrow, or conflict with any term of this
   license. This requirement applies to the Modified Version itself;
   it does not extend to independent works aggregated with it (see
   Section 5).

e. **Notices preserved** — You must keep intact all copyright notices
   and this full license text in any copy or substantial portion of a
   Covered Work you Distribute.

For the avoidance of doubt: the developer of a Modified Version
acquires no authority to grant any permission reserved to the Author
(including permission to receive Compensation or to Distribute
Unmodified Copies), whether for the original Mod, their own Modified
Version, or anyone else's. The only exception is the limited,
personal, non-transferable monetization right that Section 4 grants
directly to the developer of a Major Derivative for that Major
Derivative; that right is granted by this license itself, not by the
developer, and conveys no authority to license or permit anything to
anyone else.

## 4. No Commercial Exploitation Without Permission

Without prior Written Permission from the Author, no Covered Work may
be provided to any third party — whether by Distribution, Private
Sharing, or any other transfer — in exchange for Compensation, nor
may access to it be used to generate Compensation. Prohibited conduct
includes, without limitation:

- Selling a Covered Work or licensing it for a fee, publicly or
  privately, including delivering a commissioned or custom-built
  Modified Version to a paying person or entity (see the development-services
  exception below).
- Placing a Covered Work, or its download or source, behind any
  paywall, subscription, "supporter-only" or early-access tier, or
  mandatory donation.
- Distributing download links monetized through advertising
  link-shorteners, ad-gates, survey-gates, or similar
  revenue-generating intermediaries.
- Hosting or linking a Covered Work's download on a website or page
  that you operate or control and that is monetized through
  advertising, affiliate links, or sponsorship, where such revenue is
  attributable in whole or in part to the Covered Work.
- Enrolling a Covered Work in, or receiving payment from, any platform
  creator revenue-share, points, or payout program. Only the Author —
  and the developer of a Major Derivative, as provided below — may
  receive such payments.
- Bundling a Covered Work into any paid modpack, plugin collection,
  launcher, or server product.
- Conditioning access to a Covered Work on the purchase of any product
  or service.

The following are not prohibited by this Section:

- Incidental advertising revenue earned by an independent third-party
  hosting platform on its own pages, where no payment or revenue share
  flows to the uploader and access to the work is free and
  unconditioned.
- Voluntary, non-mandatory donations to the developer of a Modified
  Version, provided access to the Modified Version and its Complete
  Corresponding Source is in no way conditioned on, accelerated by, or
  enhanced by donating.
- Major Derivative monetization: the developer of a Major
  Derivative may, for their own public releases of that Major
  Derivative only, enroll in and receive payment from a hosting
  platform's creator revenue-share, points, or payout program, and
  receive voluntary donations, provided that: (i) the Major Derivative
  and its Complete Corresponding Source remain available free of
  charge and unconditioned — no paywall, sale, subscription, tier,
  early access, ad-gate, link-shortener, or barrier of any kind;
  (ii) all conditions of Section 3 are met, including attribution to
  the Author; and (iii) the work genuinely qualifies as a Major
  Derivative under the Preambule. This permission is personal to the
  developer who performed the qualifying work and is
  non-transferable: it does not extend to redistributors or mirrors of
  the Major Derivative, does not attach to further Modified Versions
  made by others, and does not permit selling copies, paid bundles, or
  any conduct otherwise prohibited by this Section.
- Paid development services: being paid for the labor of
  developing a Substantive Modification, provided that the resulting
  Modified Version, with its Complete Corresponding Source, is made
  publicly available under Section 3 at no charge no later than it is
  delivered to the paying person or entity, and they are charged for the
  development work only, not for the copy or for exclusive access.
- Server Operation as permitted by Section 1.
- Showcases, reviews, and links: creating monetized commentary,
  reviews, tutorials, videos, streams, or articles about a Covered
  Work, and linking (without an ad-gate, link-shortener, or similar
  intermediary) to the Author's official download page or to any
  Distribution that complies with this license. Such linking is
  neither Distribution nor prohibited Compensation. This safe harbor
  does not extend to hosting the work's files yourself.
- Anything done by the Author.

Only the Author may grant permission under this license, for the Mod
and for all Modified Versions alike.

## 5. Aggregates (Modpacks and Compilations)

Inclusion of a Covered Work in a compilation, modpack, launcher, or
distribution alongside separate and independent works does not cause
this license to apply to those other works ("mere aggregation").
However:

- The copy of the Covered Work within the aggregate must itself fully
  comply with this license: Written Permission if it is an Unmodified
  Copy (Section 2) — except as the modpack bundling permission below
  provides — the conditions of Section 3 if it is a Modified Version,
  and Section 4 in all cases.

- Modpack bundling permission (Authorized Platforms only):
  Notwithstanding Section 2, you may include an Unmodified Copy of
  the Mod in a modpack, and Distribute that modpack, without Written
  Permission, provided all of the following are met:

  a. Platform restriction — the modpack is Distributed solely on
     or through one or more Authorized Platforms, including via such
     a platform's native modpack, dependency, or file-reference
     mechanism. This permission does not extend to distributing the
     modpack, or the Mod within it, on or through any platform that
     is not an Authorized Platform, even if the modpack is also
     available on an Authorized Platform.

  b. Provenance — the included copy is an exact, unmodified copy
     of a release the Author published on an Authorized Platform, or
     is referenced or fetched from the Author's official publication
     there (as with dependency-based pack formats) rather than
     re-hosted. Referencing the official file rather than embedding a
     copy is preferred where the platform supports it.

  c. Free and unconditioned — the modpack is available free of
     charge and without any barrier prohibited by Section 4. Section
     4 fully applies; the aggregate revenue-share carve-out below
     remains available on its own terms.

  d. Attribution — the modpack's public listing or documentation
     credits the Author as the creator of the Mod and links to the
     Mod's official page on an Authorized Platform, and does not
     imply the Author endorses the modpack.

  e. Currency — if a platform ceases to be an Authorized Platform
     (see Preambule), this permission terminates prospectively for
     that platform: copies of the modpack already Distributed there
     are unaffected, but you may not publish new versions or updates
     of the modpack containing the Mod on that platform, and should
     remove or update existing listings within a reasonable time
     where the platform permits.

  This permission covers inclusion in a genuine aggregate of multiple
  independent works. It does not authorize standalone re-uploads or
  mirrors of the Mod presented as a "modpack," nor a pack whose
  primary content or selling point is the Mod itself; those remain
  governed by Section 2.
- If the aggregate as a whole is sold, paywalled, tiered, or otherwise
  monetized, the inclusion of the Covered Work in it is prohibited by
  Section 4 regardless of how the price is nominally allocated.
- Aggregate revenue-share carve-out:platform creator
  revenue-share, points, or payout payments earned by the author of a
  free, unconditioned aggregate (such as a modpack) for the aggregate
  as a whole are not prohibited Compensation with respect to a Covered
  Work included in it, provided the Covered Work is one component
  among multiple independent works, is itself freely available, and is
  included in compliance with this license. This carve-out does not
  apply where the Covered Work is the aggregate's primary content or
  selling point, and does not permit any conduct prohibited elsewhere
  in Section 4.

