## 9. Termination and Cure

Any violation of Sections 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6 automatically terminates
your rights under this license.

However, if you cease all violations, your license is reinstated
(a) provisionally, unless and until the Author expressly and finally
terminates it, and (b) permanently, if the Author fails to notify you
of the violation by reasonable means within 60 days after the
cessation. Moreover, your license is reinstated permanently if this is
the first time you have received notice of violation of this license
from the Author and you cure the violation within 30 days after
receiving the notice.

Termination of your rights does not terminate the licenses of parties
who received copies or rights from you and who remain in compliance
(see Section 10).

